SUMMARY:Buck Spring Lodge to Pilot Rock Loop - 10 Miles\, 3K Ft EG
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n**Details**\n\n* 10 Miles\, 3000 F
 t elevation gain\n* Carpool meeting time is 9:00 at the Asheville Outlets 
 parking lot behind the Waffle House.\n* Sign up starts Friday at 5pm\n\nTh
 is is a nice loop that starts at the Mt Pisgah Overlook by Buck Spring Lod
 ge and goes down Laurel Mtn trail to Slate Rock Creek trail and then out a
 nd back to a really nice rock overlook. We will have a snack there before 
 starting back with the main part of the climb towards the end of the hike 
 There is another rock overlook along the way back up where we will briefly
  stop. We will do a moderate pace of about 2.7 mph but stop for breaks as 
 needed. PLEASE BE IN SHAPE AND CAPABLE OF HIKING THIS DISTANCE AND ELEVATI
 ON.\n\nhttps://www.alltrails.com/explore/custom-routes/uploaded-route-6184
 bd7\n\n**CARPOOL**\nWe will meet at the Asheville Outlets behind the Waffl
 e House at 9:00. Please be there a little early so we can leave at 9:00 fo
 r the trailhead. If you plan to meet us at the Buck Spring/Mt Pisgah Overl
 ook\, plan to be there by 9:30.\n\n**WEATHER**\nI'll watch the weather and
  post a cancellation message by 7:00 AM if the forecast is >50% chance of 
 precipitation.\n\n**QUESTIONS?**\nYou can message me through MeetUp until 
 9:00 AM the day of. Cell reception may be sketchy\, but you can try to tex
 t or call me up to the start of the hike: (508) 965-2333.\n\n**LEGALESE**\
 nThis Asheville Hiking Group event involves hiking and\, possibly\, transp
 ortation to and from the meetup site. Participants are responsible for the
 ir own safety and affirm that they have the appropriate skills\, physical 
 conditioning\, equipment\, and supplies. Hiking may involve risks to onese
 lf and property. Neither your hike organizer nor Asheville Hiking Group ca
 n assure your safety nor eliminate all risks. Participants assume full res
 ponsibility for any injuries\, damages\, or losses.
