SUMMARY:Scenic AVL #8: Beaver Lake to Reynolds Mountain
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nThis route goes up Reynolds Mounta
 in and rambles along the ridge line. We do not go around Beaver Lake becau
 se of their dog rules.\n\n**Rating:** Strenuous (climb up Reynolds is stee
 p)\n**Distance:** 6 miles\n**Elevation Gain:** 1000 ft\n**Surface:** Road\
 n**Pace:** 3.2 mph\, best effort on push up Reynolds\n**Features:** Lake v
 iews\, mountain views\n**Bears:** Not likely\n**Dogs:** On leash\n**Gear:*
 * in winter\, please bring a headlamp. In summer\, this hike is very hot a
 nd exposed\, so bring water and/or a hat. No flip-flops.\n\n**Parking is l
 imited** at the triangle\, but there is overflow parking available at Beav
 er Lake Bird Sanctuary. If you park at Beaver Lake Bird Sanctuary\, CALL t
 he hike leader at 828-290-0886 and let me know. Please walk to the Triangl
 e to join the group. Alternatively\, arrange a car pool from Ingles on Mer
 rimon with others in the group by making a note in the comments below.\n\n
 **Route:** [Reynold's Mountain Winter Route](https://www.alltrails.com/exp
 lore/map/reynolds-mountain-winter-version-43fa7f5?u=i&sh=ifwm3x)\n\n**Scen
 ic Asheville Series:** There are [9 hikes in the series](https://docs.goog
 le.com/document/d/11ewlUM9OV8I4npc1cNNsSYOnXI0QPw2isAleXdFzEbI/edit?usp=sh
 aring)\; hike them all and receive an[ attractive badge](https://docs.goog
 le.com/drawings/d/1goXUXfzUBqhB4_UeCxodlk4ZPeCCgqZrWK2EUJvk_vI/edit?usp=sh
 aring) for your backpack. Check your progress **[HERE](https://docs.google
 .com/spreadsheets/d/1XUm-X1_OhxKIi8JU5rhjsW37cAl4yYx8yB_NEjjI5Lk/edit?gid=
 0#gid=0).**\nSpecial bonus for badge holders: You can always come on a hik
 e\, even if you are on the wait list. See our [highlights here](https://do
 cs.google.com/presentation/d/18cFp2Uhw8XthOFXxekBpt2LGP6ww-V7kmXQExI7Y0h0/
 )!\n\n**Wait List:** If someone is waiting on a particular hike for their 
 badge\, they may be moved to Going ahead of other people. If I notice you 
 need one more hike for your badge\, I may auto-add you to the hike.\n\n**G
 uests:** If you bring a guest\, please add them as a plus one on the app s
 o it will add them to the count of attendees. Make sure your guest knows t
 he distance and elevation gain\, and carries appropriate gear (water\, hea
 dlamp in winter). Also\, if someone comes as a guest\, it won't count towa
 rd a badge\, because I won't have record of their name (unless you text it
  to me or otherwise make special effort so that I know they attended).\n\n
 **RSVP and On-Time Start:**\n\n* If you decide you cannot come\, please ch
 ange your RSVP\n* If you must cancel\, please change your status to "Not G
 oing" as soon as possible so wait-listers can have sufficient notice.\n* T
 here are generally 1 or 2 no-shows on my hikes\, so we don't wait for peop
 le to arrive. If you are late\, you'll be left behind. In some hikes\, the
 re are "if late" instructions to intercept us.\n* Notes and comments are g
 enuinely appreciated.\n\n**Disclaimer and Release of Liability:**\nThis ac
 tivity involves hiking on city streets that may have traffic. Participants
  are responsible for their safety on streets and trails. The organizer of 
 this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The function of the
  organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or participate in
  this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily agree to assum
 e all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising from\, as a resu
 lt of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you acknowledge that
  you agree to the Meetup terms: https://www.meetup.com/terms
